{"event": "agent", "step": 111, "message": {"type": "bug_report", "screen": "Shop > Sell > Sell Old Gear sheet and per-item sell panel", "element": "Iron Sword row (Sell Old Gear sheet) and Sell: Iron Sword quantity control", "element_ref": 20, "field": "Quantity offered for multi-copy gear", "symptom_type": "wrong_value", "expected": "With \"Keep one of each item\" OFF, all unequipped copies are offered: Iron Sword ×3 (186 coins) and Bronze Axe ×2 (50 coins) in Sell Old Gear; the per-item panel's Max is 3. Only the toggle ON should reserve one copy.", "observed": "With the toggle OFF, Sell Old Gear lists \"Iron Sword ×2 124\" and \"Bronze Axe ×1 25\", total 5,416. The per-item panel for Iron Sword opens at 2 with Max and + disabled, and Bronze Axe offers no quantity control (max 1). The same rows appear with the toggle ON, so the toggle makes no difference to multi-copy gear. Sell Junk does honour the toggle (Cowhide ×14 → ×13 when ON).", "observed_quote": "Iron Sword ×2 124", "steps": ["Open Shop, tap Sell tab. Confirm Keep one of each item is OFF.", "Inventory has Iron Sword ×3 in inventory (plus one equipped) and Bronze Axe ×2 in inventory (plus one equipped).", "Tap Sell Old Gear. Observe Iron Sword ×2 (124) and Bronze Axe ×1 (25), Total 5,416.", "Tap the Iron Sword row. The sell panel opens at quantity 2; Increase and Max are disabled.", "Turn Keep one of each item ON. Tap Sell Old Gear again: the same Iron Sword ×2 and Bronze Axe ×1 rows appear, total 149 only if the gear list is filtered, with no change from OFF for these two items."], "anchor_node": {"class": "android.view.View", "contains": ["Enemies"], "bounds": [292, 495, 686, 621]}}}
